v 3
d projectbuilder: scaffold a data-analysis project folder with a numbered do-file pipeline
d
d projectbuilder builds a project folder in one command: a raw-data
d folder, an analytic-data folder, an output folder, a documentation
d folder, and a numbered do-file pipeline (000_control through
d 600_analysis). A control file holds every path in one place and can
d run the whole pipeline. If you already have the data, point data() at
d local files or url() at a source address and projectbuilder copies it
d in and writes a documentation page; with the optional convertanything
d and combineall installed it also converts each raw file and appends
d them into one analytic file. If the data comes later, scaffold now and rerun
d with rebuild on every refresh; rebuild never overwrites a do-file you
d have edited unless you add replace. The tool is self-contained (every
d file is written by the program, no template folder), uses only Stata's
d cross-platform file commands, and never overwrites an existing project.
d
d Optional companions add power when installed but are never required:
d convertanything and combineall (author's GitHub), descsave (SSC),
d srctag/srcfind (author's GitHub), and webdoc2 (author's GitHub).
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer.
d
d The command leaves the dataset in memory untouched.
d
d v2.1.0: the webdoc2 documentation render is self-contained (a fallback
d header ships inside every project; no extra fetch or adopath step); the
d new sitebuild subcommand writes a catalog page across every project
d under a folder; the new check subcommand reports every optional
d companion in one table with clickable install commands; the generated
d control file logs per-stage runtimes to run_log.txt; and raw files are
d checksummed so a rebuild reports which are new, changed, or unchanged.
d
d A test battery ships with the package as an ancillary file; retrieve it
d with -net get projectbuilder- and run it with
d -do test_projectbuilder.do-.
d
d Authors: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d          Elizabeth Teas, Sr Research Scientist, Far Harbor, LLC
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260808
d
f projectbuilder.ado
f projectbuilder.sthlp
f test_projectbuilder.do
